s about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "a great variety of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-fd22601090", "expression": "a vast amount of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "a vast amount of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-6cd703393b", "expression": "a wide range of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "a wide range of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-9f6ba5ad60", "expression": "all kinds of dessert, especially", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "all kinds of dessert, especially This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-7b46615955", "expression": "In general, ... I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use In general, ... I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who to [situation-appropriate completion of the template]", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Template pattern: fill the placeholder with topic-relevant content. Used to Used to mark your answer as personal viewpoint, especially in Part 1 and Part 3", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, clearly marks personal stance", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "In general, ... I'm pretty sure I'm not the only one who For example, this is a great way to introduce your point naturally.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B2", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-be9ec5b394", "expression": "plenty of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "plenty of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "A2", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-7df519c54e", "expression": "There are lots of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "There are lots of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-bb377df93d", "expression": "There are plenty of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to introduce a broad observation", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to make broader observations about trends or patterns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows ability to identify patterns", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "There are plenty of This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-015"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["generalisation"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-eb2e70d88b", "expression": "Apart from that, when it comes to", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a new clause to introduce supplementary information", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to extend a response with related supporting details", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, extends responses naturally", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "Apart from that, when it comes to This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "A2", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-93770a7dc0", "expression": "As far as ... goes,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "As far as [topic] goes, [personal opinion or observation]...", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Template pattern: fill the placeholder with topic-relevant content. Used to Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As far as ... goes For example, this is a great way to introduce your point naturally.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-6a9c2ca318", "expression": "As far as ... is concerned,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "As far as [topic] is concerned, [statement]...", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Template pattern: fill the placeholder with topic-relevant content. Used to Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As far as ... is concerned For example, this is a great way to introduce your point naturally.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-04c2a32eae", "expression": "As for", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a sentence to focus attention on a specific aspect", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for my future plans, I hope to pursue a master's degree abroad.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "A2", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-46ecd5d1ff", "expression": "As for me,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a sentence to focus attention on a specific aspect", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for me This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-05ae977a7d", "expression": "As for students, we might feel", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a sentence to focus attention on a specific aspect", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for students, we might feel This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-6795992e23", "expression": "As for the reason why,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use within or at the start of a clause expressing causality", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to explain reasoning, especially in Part 3 analytical responses", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, demonstrates logical reasoning ability", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for the reason why This explains why the situation has changed so dramatically.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-2d4705cc1d", "expression": "As for the reason why, it's simply because", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use within or at the start of a clause expressing causality", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to explain reasoning, especially in Part 3 analytical responses", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "informal, conversational, natural, demonstrates logical reasoning ability", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for the reason why, it's simply because This explains why the situation has changed so dramatically.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-aef73ed66c", "expression": "As for the reason(s), I'd say", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a clause to signal personal viewpoint", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to mark your answer as personal viewpoint, especially in Part 1 and Part 3", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, clearly marks personal stance", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "As for the reason(s), I'd say technology has fundamentally changed the way we communicate with each other.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-f3f8447c47", "expression": "First off, in terms of", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the beginning of a clause to order multiple points", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to structure multi-point answers, especially in Part 2 long turns", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, improves coherence and cohesion scores", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "First off, in terms of I'll explain my reasons step by step.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "A2", "categoryIds": ["cat-016"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["topic-introduction"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-814b0dc0a8", "expression": "If we're talking about", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a sentence to focus attention on a specific aspect", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to narrow focus to a specific aspect of the question", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, signals topic management skills", "zh": ""}, "e