ic,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use before a precise detail or clarification", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used when you want to give precise details rather than general statements", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, adds precision and detail", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "To be specific This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-019"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["specification"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-e727b572b6", "expression": "Could you please clarify", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use when needing the interlocutor to repeat, explain, or elaborate", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used when you did not hear or understand the question fully", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, shows active listening and communication skills", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "Could you please clarify This is a useful expression for expressing yourself naturally in English.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "A2", "categoryIds": ["cat-020"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["clarification"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-dbbb1e1363", "expression": "What do you mean by", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a clause to signal personal viewpoint", "zh": ""}, "contexts": {"en": "Used to mark your answer as personal viewpoint, especially in Part 1 and Part 3", "zh": ""}, "connotation": {"en": "semi-formal, appropriate for IELTS context, clearly marks personal stance", "zh": ""}, "example": {"en": "What do you mean by technology has fundamentally changed the way we communicate with each other.", "zh": ""}, "cefr": "B1", "categoryIds": ["cat-020"], "subfunctionIds": [], "chainIds": [], "tags": ["clarification"], "seeAlso": []}, {"id": "dm-84ba9d9c4c", "expression": "As for society as a whole,", "variants": [], "collocation": {"en": "Use at the start of a sente